WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.282
Family loans can be generous, but dates, payments, and balances get hard to track over time.

2
00:00:06.732 --> 00:00:14.085
Family Loan Ledger is for parents and relatives who lend, and adult children who want a clear view of what they owe.

3
00:00:14.535 --> 00:00:20.867
Set up a ledger for each borrower. Record the amount, purpose, agreed rate, and start date.

4
00:00:21.317 --> 00:00:28.777
Add loans, payments, or adjustments as they happen. Dated entries keep the running balance easy to follow.

5
00:00:29.227 --> 00:00:36.766
Interest and activity stay together in one ledger, so the history isn’t scattered across texts, notes, and spreadsheets.

6
00:00:37.216 --> 00:00:45.299
Administrators manage accounts and entries; borrowers review their own ledger in read-only view, seeing the same record.

7
00:00:45.749 --> 00:00:53.237
For a first-home loan, a parent records each loan and payment; the borrower can follow the balance over time.

8
00:00:53.687 --> 00:01:01.917
Family Loan Ledger keeps family loan records clear and organized. Explore the demo at familyloanledger.com.


